Reproduction
Compile browser/navigation-check.zero with the original Zero compiler --host
and execute it. Each case prints PASS or FAIL; a failed assertion exits1.
The checked source is embedded between BROWSER ADDRESS CHECK, BROWSER UI CHECK
and BROWSER RENDER CHECK markers. Refresh the copies from their production
fragments after edits; UI includes the actual address, parse and render parts.

Remaining limits
Fragments currently preserve the URL and refetch; in-page anchor scrolling is
not implemented. DNS/host validation and connection errors belong to the
transport. TLS, CSS, JavaScript, browser security isolation and full website
compatibility are not established by this report. Native checks supplement,
rather than replace, the BIOS/UEFI and actual keyboard/display VM tests.
